        {
          "name": "GovernorBravo Governance",
          "value": "$0 reachable",
          "description": "governance · Immutable — On-chain governance contract (GovernorBravoDelegator) that proposes and votes on changes to the Timelock. UNI token holders vote on proposals that, if passed, are queued in the 48-hour Timelock. In practice, the only meaningful action available is controlling the protocol fee switch — all core contracts are immutable."
        },
        {
          "name": "Governance Timelock (48h)",
          "value": "$0 reachable",
          "description": "governance · Immutable — Timelock contract with a 48-hour minimum delay, controlled by GovernorBravo (eth:0x408E...24C3). Owns FeeToSetter and FeeTo, giving it the ability to change the protocol fee recipient address and toggle the 0.05% protocol fee on liquidity pools. Cannot modify swap logic, pool contracts, or the factory."
        }
      ],
